# power.manifest — config owned by mod_power (power management).
#
# Three layers, two of them tracked here (update-system.md phase 2):
#   • /usr/share/w/defaults/power.schema — WHO may set each key. Shipped data,
#     class managed: W owns it, every update overwrites it.
#   • /etc/w/power.conf — the admin's DEVIATIONS from the vendor defaults. Class
#     override: the update never touches it; `w-reset power` drops the deviations
#     so the machine falls back to the vendor layer ("as on a fresh install").
#
# NOT tracked here — generated output, regenerate with `sudo w-power apply`:
#   • /usr/share/w/defaults/power.conf      (the vendor layer itself: w-power
#     writes it from preset_sys()/preset_idle() for this machine's MODE, so it has
#     no source file in the repo — same precedent as the rendered nodes below)
#   • ~/.config/hypr/hypridle.conf          (idle timers; moved off mod_hyprland)
#   • /etc/systemd/logind.conf.d/10-w-power.conf   (lid / power key)
#   • the battery charge threshold sysfs (via w-charge-limit.service)
# ~/.config/w/power.conf holds only per-user idle overrides, created on demand
# with no vendor default — class user-conf: `w-reset power` deletes it (its
# "default" IS absence). Re-rendering hypridle.conf from the drop still needs a
# root `w-power apply` (see `reset_module`'s power/nightlight re-render step).
#
# Format: <path>\t<class>   class: managed | override | user-conf
/usr/share/w/defaults/power.schema	managed
/etc/w/power.conf	override
.config/w/power.conf	user-conf
